# "NOT WALKED YET" IS NOT "YOUR LIBRARY IS CLEAN".
#
# No clusters, `scan_complete: false`. Perceptual hashes are computed by a pass,
# and a library the pass has not finished walking has no clusters for a reason
# that has nothing to do with duplicates. The screen has to say so, because the
# alternative — "No duplicates found" — is a claim the vault has not earned, and
# a member who reads it stops looking.
#
# `total_reclaimable_bytes: 0` is honest here for the same reason and NOT a
# separate signal: nothing has been measured, so nothing can be promised. A
# screen must not read this zero as "there is nothing to gain"; it is
# `scan_complete` that licenses that sentence.
#
# This is data, not a failure. The read landed and returned the true current
# state of a pass in progress, and a retry does not make a pass finish sooner.
seat {
  availability: AVAILABILITY_READY
  durability: DURABILITY_AUTHORITATIVE
  connectivity: CONNECTIVITY_ONLINE_UNMETERED
}
data {
  scan_complete: false
}
